==Battleground==
*1 [[Pastry Cat (Enemy)|Pastry Cat]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*3 [[Unicycle Cat (Enemy)|Unicycle Cats]] (100%) spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Unicycle Cat (Enemy)|Unicycle Cat]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Beefcake Cat (Enemy)|Beefcake Cats]] spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Heavy Assault C.A.T. (Enemy)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]] spawns.
**1 [[Ultimate Bondage Cat (Enemy)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]] spawns.
**1 [[Ultimate Bondage Cat (Enemy)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]] spawns.
**1 [[Unicycle Cat (Enemy)|Unicycle Cat]] (100%) spawns.
**1 [[Dancer Cat (Enemy)|Dancer Cat]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] Battle Item is recommended to mitigate much of the stalling you'll have to do in the opening.

Pastry Cat is very tanky, and you can take advantage of that to build up a small stack of [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]] and optionally [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeyes]] during the opening phase of the fight. Good meatshielding is required to prevent them from pushing, so bring at least 3 in the form of [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] and two other cheap meatshields. Once you have enough money, send out [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] to start chipping away at the enemies. Continue this cycle until eventually you kill both of the Unicycle Cats, then push Pastry back to the enemy base.

At this point, your goal is simple: clear out the initial horde of enemies using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]]. This combination of enemies pushes very hard, so bring a [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] if you're not able to keep up with the spamming. Once the Beefcake Cats come out, cycle out [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to get rid of them as soon as humanly possible. Any strong backline Ubers you have will be a godsend here.

Eventually, you'll reach a stable point where you can shift your focus over to slowly sniping the enemy base with your Long Distance attackers. You shouldn't struggle with the cleanup if you survived the initial outbreak.

